    "# Notebook 7 — Next-month pick count per SKU (two years of history)\n",
    "\n",
    "**Church & Dwight | York Distribution Center**\n",
    "\n",
    "**What it forecasts.** The number of times each SKU will be picked over the next 28 days. One row in the pick files is one pick, so the target is a count of rows (every customer-order pick, all zones and units of measure).\n",
    "\n",
    "**What changed in this version.**\n",
    "\n",
    "| | Before | **Now** |\n",
    "|---|---|---|\n",
    "| **Input** | your preprocessed `sku_day_panel.csv` (one year) | **the raw pick files directly**: it reads every `.csv` in your `raw_data` folder (the new `YOWMSPD2_Pick_Data_SEP2024thruSep2025.csv` plus the two 2025-26 files), applies the same rules as your preprocessing script, and builds the daily counts itself |\n",
    "| **History** | Sep 2025 to Sep 2026 | **Sep 2024 to Sep 2026** (about 2 years) |\n",
    "| **Seasonality** | not possible with one year | **last-year features are now live**: how this SKU, and the whole warehouse, changed between the month before this window and this window a year ago |\n",
    "| **Development origins** | 12 (about 6 months) | **26 (a full year)**, so every season is tested |\n",
    "\n",
    "**How the model works (unchanged).** For every SKU, LightGBM predicts next month's pick count *as a multiplier on last month's count*. That is blended with plain \"last 28 days\", and the blend is **chosen separately for each consistency group** (Steady / Variable / Erratic / Rare), with the choice scored leave-one-origin-out so the reported accuracy is not flattered. The latest 28 days are a locked test.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Rules applied to the raw files** (same as your preprocessing script): keep only rows with a non-blank `CUST_NAME` (customer-order picks); drop any transaction number (`NO`) that appears in more than one file (the new file and the 2025-26 archive share the week of Sep 21-26, 2025); drop the first and last calendar day because they are partial; fill missing SKU-days with zero.\n",
    "\n",
    "> **How to run:** put the raw files in the folder set below, edit `DATA_DIR` if needed, then Kernel → Restart & Run All. Reading the raw files takes about a minute; later runs can reuse a cache (see `REBUILD_FROM_RAW`). If LightGBM is missing: `%pip install lightgbm` and restart."
   ]
  },
