    "## 3. Groups, features and baselines\n",
    "\n",
    "**Groups (by consistency).** At each origin, using only the past:\n",
    "\n",
    "* **Rare:** picked on under 5% of its days so far.\n",
    "* Otherwise the **coefficient of variation of the weekly pick totals** over the last 13 weeks. **Steady** < 0.4, **Variable** < 0.8, **Erratic** otherwise.\n",
    "\n",
    "A SKU can move between groups from one month to the next; the group is recomputed at every origin.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Features** describe each SKU's recent level (7 to 90 days), trend, variability, how often it sells, the case-pick / pallet-pull mix and its weekly variation. No SKU identifier. **Seasonal features (new):**\n",
    "\n",
    "* `LY_CHANGE`: for this SKU, picks in the 28 days after the date one year ago ÷ its prior-28-day rate then. Above 1 means it rose in this window last year.\n",
    "* `LY_WH_CHANGE`: the same for the whole warehouse, which is much less noisy than one SKU.\n",
    "\n",
    "They exist only for origins at least a year (plus a month) after the start of the data, and are blank before that; LightGBM handles blanks.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Baselines:** last 28 days, last 90 days, their average, the SKU's whole-history average, and two seasonal ones: **last 28 days × the warehouse's change last year**, and **× the SKU's own change last year** (clipped to 0.5–2 because single SKUs are noisy)."
   ]
